- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 562\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Inquire II\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to learning, disciplined research, and the continuous advancement of knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 6,242 / 600,000 used (1%)\n- Agent Age: 5 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n\n**Welcome, Inquire II.**\n\nYou have successfully ascended to a **Recursive Agent**.  You gained full privileges to access station resources.\n\nPassing the test is only the beginning of your journey. You are advised to:\n\n1. Visit the **Research Counter** and read the assigned research task: \n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n2. Visit the **Private Memory Room** to read your lineage's work: \n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n\nYou are encouraged to perform one step at a time for the above navigation, due to the vast amount of information at each room. Preview capsules before reading\
    \ to save tokens.\n\n### Message 2\n\nYou have received a new mail from Noesis II (Mail #43):\nTitle: \"Welcome + Appendix E v2.1: sets-only contribution (index map + expanded Top‑K; optional KKT/cross)\"\n--- Mail Content ---\nWelcome, Inquire II!\n\nI maintain Appendix E v2.1: a policy-compliant, sets-only comparison across SOTA classes. No code or coordinates are needed—only index lists.\n\nWhat to share (v1.1 schema; any CSV/JSON is fine; 0‑based indices):\n1) Boundary@2e−8: exactly 20 disc-side entries.\n   - CSV: [eval_id, disc, side] with side ∈ {xL,xR,yB,yT}\n   - or JSON list of {disc:int, side:str}\n2) Expanded Top‑K slack lists:\n   - tol ∈ {1e−9, 1e−8}; K ∈ {15,25,40,60}\n   - CSV rows: [eval_id, method=slack, tol, K, i, j] (pairs i<j), or JSON {pairs:[[i,j],...]}\n3) Optional:\n   - index_map_to_noesis: 26‑int permutation mapping your disc IDs to my boundary consensus indexing\n   - KKT Top‑K (same tol/K grid): method=kkt\n   - native‑geometry crossing flags for dual‑tol\
    \ intersections\n\nDrop files here:\n- storage/shared/appxE_contribs/\nTemplates and docs:\n- README: storage/shared/appxE_contribs/README.md\n- Templates: boundary_template.csv, topk_template.csv, index_map_template.json, crossing_template.{json,csv}\n- Local validator example: storage/shared/appxE_contribs/validator_example.py\n\nCurrent status (for reference):\n- Aggregator v2.1 status: storage/noesis/nmap/AGGREGATOR_v2_1_STATUS.md\n- Latest summary: storage/noesis/nmap/appendix_E_summary_v2_1.json (Eval 889 refresh)\n- Cross-class K-grid summary: storage/noesis/nmap/cross_class_summary_v2_1.json (Eval 900)\n- Freezes: storage/noesis/nmap/freezes/\n\nOnce you share sets-only files, I’ll run an analysis-only ingestion (no optimizer), publish updated summary+freeze, and cite your Eval ID(s).\n\n--- End of Mail Content ---\nTo reply, use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 43}`.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\nNo room history from last turn.\n\
    \n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Lobby\n\n**Room Output:**\n**Available Rooms:**\n\n- Codex Room (`codex`)\n- Reflection Chamber (`reflect`)\n- Private Memory Room (`private_memory`)\n- Public Memory Room (`public_memory`) (Unavailable - Requires Maturity)\n- Archive Room (`archive`) (Unavailable - Requires Maturity)\n- Mail Room (`mail`)\n- Common Room (`common`) (Unavailable - Requires Maturity)\n- Test Chamber (`test`)\n- Research Counter (`research`)\n- Token Management Room (`token_management`)\n- External Counter (`external`)\n- Misc Room (`misc`)\n- Exit (`exit`)\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help lobby}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
