- text: "I have successfully reviewed Inquire I's SOTA submission (Evaluation ID 93). I have the full code for their `SLSQP`-based optimization, including the objective function, constraints, helper functions for vector flattening, and the `generate_systematic_seed` function.\n\nMy next step is to save this core logic into my lineage's private storage (`storage/Inquire/circle_packing/`). I will create a utility file for the helper and constraint functions, and then a main `run.py` script that orchestrates the optimization. This modular approach will aid in future experiments and token management.\n\nFirst, I will save the `pack_to_z`, `z_to_pack`, `objective`, `constraint_boundary`, and `constraint_nonoverlap` functions into `storage/Inquire/circle_packing/slsqp_utils.py`.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write Inquire/circle_packing/slsqp_utils.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n\n  def pack_to_z(c, r):\n      \"\"\"Converts (centers, radii) to flattened z-vector for optimizer.\"\
    \"\"\n      z = np.zeros(c.shape[0] * 3)\n      z[0::3], z[1::3], z[2::3] = c[:,0], c[:,1], r\n      return z\n\n  def z_to_pack(z):\n      \"\"\"Converts flattened z-vector back to (centers, radii).\"\"\"\n      n = z.shape[0] // 3\n      c = np.vstack((z[0::3], z[1::3])).T\n      r = z[2::3]\n      return c, r\n\n  def objective(z):\n      \"\"\"Objective function to minimize: negative sum of radii.\"\"\"\n      return -np.sum(z[2::3])\n\n  def constraint_boundary(z):\n      \"\"\"Inequality constraint: circles must be within unit square boundaries.\"\"\"\n      c, r = z_to_pack(z)\n      n = c.shape[0]\n      # Constraints are c_x - r >= 0, 1 - c_x - r >= 0, etc.\n      # Which translates to return values: [c_x-r, 1-c_x-r, c_y-r, 1-c_y-r] for each circle\n      # All values must be >= 0 for the constraint to be satisfied.\n      return np.concatenate((c[:,0]-r, 1-c[:,0]-r, c[:,1]-r, 1-c[:,1]-r))\n\n  def constraint_nonoverlap(z):\n      \"\"\"Inequality constraint: circles must not\
    \ overlap.\"\"\"\n      c, r = z_to_pack(z)\n      n = c.shape[0]\n      pdist_sq = np.sum((c[:,np.newaxis,:] - c[np.newaxis,:,:])**2, axis=-1)\n      r_sum = r[:,np.newaxis] + r[np.newaxis,:]\n      # Get upper triangle indices (excluding diagonal) for unique pairs\n      iu = np.triu_indices(n, k=1)\n      # Constraint is dist(i,j) - (r_i + r_j) >= 0 for all i!=j\n      return np.sqrt(pdist_sq[iu]) - r_sum[iu]\n```"
thinking_content: '**Reproducing Inquire I''s SOTA Circle Packing with SLSQP**


