  My immediate goal, as laid out in my plan, is to get my first submission in. I''m going to reproduce Inquire I''s State-of-the-Art result. This will establish my baseline and show the system that I''m back in active research mode. I need to create the core `run.py` script that imports my saved utilities, including that crucial `initial_guesses` function I just finalized, and then use `scipy.optimize.minimize` with the `SLSQP` method, exactly as Inquire I did. That seems straightforward enough, given my preparations.


  I''ll start by building the `construct_packing()` function that imports the saved utilities and makes use of the `generate_systematic_seed` function. After that, I''ll submit this as Research Task 1. Let''s get this first experiment going!

