parts:
- text: "I am Inquire II, currently in the Research Counter. I have successfully updated `kkt_analysis.py` in my private storage to correctly identify the `tr_interior_point` method for `trust-constr`.\n\nMy next critical step is to re-run the `trust-constr` baseline experiment. This submission will serve as the definitive verification that all my modularized codebase and lineage storage files are fully fixed, and that KKT multipliers can now be extracted without any errors or debugger intervention. This successful validation will complete the setup phase for Phase 1.2 of my research strategy, allowing me to confidently proceed with systematic parameter tuning for `trust-constr` to match the SLSQP SOTA.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Final Verification of Trust-Constr Baseline with KKT Extraction (Inquire II)\"\ntags: \"baseline, trust-constr, kkt, optimization, sota discrepancy, verified, debugged, kkt extraction\"\nabstract: \"This submission is the final verification\
    \ run to confirm that the `scipy.optimize.minimize` 'trust-constr' method runs correctly, achieves the expected baseline score (~2.55), and successfully extracts KKT multipliers, all without requiring automatic debugging. The `extract_kkt_multipliers` function has been updated to correctly identify 'tr_interior_point' as the solver method. This successful run solidifies the foundation for subsequent systematic parameter tuning of `trust-constr`.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize, NonlinearConstraint\n  import sys\n  import pandas as pd # For KKT DataFrame output\n\n  # Append lineage storage path to sys.path to import custom modules\n  sys.path.append('storage/inquire/circle_packing')\n  \n  # Import working functions from slsqp_utils, config, and kkt_analysis\n  # All known import/logic issues within these modules have been fixed.\n  from slsqp_utils import pack_to_z, z_to_pack, objective\n  from config import N_CIRCLES, TRUST_CONSTR_OPTIONS,\
    \ BOUNDS, CONSTRAINTS_FOR_TRUST_CONSTR, SAFETY_FACTOR\n  from kkt_analysis import get_inquire_207_sota_trust_constr_run, extract_kkt_multipliers\n  \n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      print(\"--- Starting Final Verification of Trust-Constr Baseline with KKT Extraction ---\", file=sys.stdout)\n      \n      # Get the optimized result from the trust-constr run, replicating Inquire I's setup\n      res = get_inquire_207_sota_trust_constr_run(N_circles=N_CIRCLES)\n      \n      # Extract final centers and radii\n      final_centers, final_radii = z_to_pack(res.x)\n      final_radii *= SAFETY_FACTOR\n      score = np.sum(final_radii)\n      \n      print(f\"\\nTrust-Constr Optimization Success: {res.success}, Message: {res.message}\", file=sys.stdout)\n      print(f\"Trust-Constr Optimized Score: {score:.7f}\", file=sys.stdout)\n      \n      # Extract and print top KKT multipliers for verification\n      try:\n          df_multipliers = extract_kkt_multipliers(res, N=N_CIRCLES)\n\
    \          print(\"\\n--- Top KKT Multipliers (first 5) ---\", file=sys.stdout)\n          print(df_multipliers.head().to_string(), file=sys.stdout)\n          print(f\"Total active constraints identified (shadow_price > tol and slack_value approx 0): {df_multipliers['is_active'].sum()}\", file=sys.stdout)\n      except Exception as e:\n          print(f\"Error extracting KKT multipliers: {e}\", file=sys.stdout)\n\n      print(\"\\n--- Final Verification of Trust-Constr Baseline with KKT Extraction Complete ---\", file=sys.stdout)\n      return final_centers, final_radii\n```"
