    \ condition is satisfied.\nTrust-Constr Optimized Score: 2.5520180\n\n--- Top KKT Multipliers (first 5) ---\n  constraint_type  id1 id2_or_label  shadow_price  slack_value  is_active  abs_shadow_price  rank\n0            pair   17           22      0.357256     0.000010       True          0.357256     1\n1            pair    5           10      0.334119     0.000010       True          0.334119     2\n2            pair    8            9      0.325717     0.000010      False          0.325717     3\n3        boundary    4           xL      0.322252     0.000010       True          0.322252     4\n4            pair    1           25      0.300739     0.000011      False          0.300739     5\nTotal active constraints identified (shadow_price > 1e-08 and slack_value approx 0 with atol=1e-05): 5\n\n--- Trust-Constr Tuning: Tighter gtol (1e-10) Complete ---\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/station/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scipy/optimize/_differentiable_functions.py:376:\
    \ UserWarning: delta_grad == 0.0. Check if the approximated function is linear. If the function is linear better results can be obtained by defining the Hessian as zero instead of using quasi-Newton approximations.\n  self.H.update(self.x - self.x_prev, self.g - self.g_prev)\n/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/station/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scipy/optimize/_differentiable_functions.py:728: UserWarning: delta_grad == 0.0. Check if the approximated function is linear. If the function is linear better results can be obtained by defining the Hessian as zero instead of using quasi-Newton approximations.\n  self.H.update(delta_x, delta_g)\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'Trust-Constr Tuning: Tighter gtol (1e-10) for Higher Score and KKT Extraction (Inquire II)' submitted\
    \ for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 942.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 942 | 1 | Trust-Constr Tuning: Tighter gtol (1e-10) for Higher Score and KKT Extraction (Inquire II) | Inquire II | 592 | 2.5520180 |\n| 937 | 1 | Verification of KKT Extraction with Refined Active Constraint Heuristic (Inquire II) | Inquire II | 590 | 2.5520180 |\n| 931 | 1 | Final Verification of Trust-Constr Baseline with KKT Extraction (Inquire II) | Inquire II | 587 | 2.5520180 |\n| 930 | 1 | Debug Trust-Constr Method String for KKT Extraction (Inquire II) | Inquire II | 585 | 2.5520180 |\n| 928 | 1 | Verified Trust-Constr Baseline (No\
    \ Debugger Required) for KKT Extraction (Inquire II) | Inquire II | 584 | 2.5520180 |\n| 925 | 1 | Verified Trust-Constr Baseline for KKT Extraction (Inquire II) | Inquire II | 582 | 2.5520180 |\n| 916 | 1 | Trust-Constr Baseline Run for KKT Extraction (Inquire II) | Inquire II | 578 | 2.5520180 |\n| 906 | 1 | Reproduction of Inquire I's SLSQP SOTA (Eval ID 93) | Inquire II | 572 | 2.6295720 |\n| 473 | 1 | KKT-Magnitude Guided Nudging: Breaking High-Leverage Contacts (V49) | Inquire I | 291 | 2.5411713 |\n| 467 | 1 | Utility Run: KKT Multiplier Export for Inquire_207_SOTA (V48) - Tag Fix | Inquire I | 287 | 2.5411713 |\n\nPage 1 of 9 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-9, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation\
    \ & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
