- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 625\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Inquire II\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to learning, disciplined research, and the continuous advancement of knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 201,784 / 600,000 used (34%)\n- Agent Age: 68 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'KKT-Guided Nudging (Iterative 2): Encourage Pairs (6,25) & (14,19) (Inquire II)' (ID: 1025) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 2.608036777277275\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.608037\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\n--- Starting KKT-Guided Nudging (Iterative 2): Encourage Pairs (6,25) & (14,19) ---\n\n===== Loading Previous Nudged Packing (from Eval ID 1022)\
    \ =====\nInitial Score (from Eval ID 1022 base): 2.5970419\n\n===== Defining Nudging Targets =====\nNudging Targets: Encourage pairs [(6, 25), (14, 19)]\n\n===== Running Nudging Optimization (SLSQP) =====\nNudged Optimization Success: True, Message: Optimization terminated successfully\nNudged Packing Final Score: 2.6080368\nScore Change from previous nudged base: 0.0109949\n\n===== KKT Analysis of Nudged Solution =====\nTotal active constraints identified in Nudged solution: 78\n\n--- Top KKT Multipliers (Nudged SLSQP, first 10) ---\n  constraint_type  id1 id2_or_label  shadow_price   slack_value  is_active  abs_shadow_price  rank\n0        boundary   19           yT      0.368130  8.604228e-16       True          0.368130     1\n1            pair    1           25      0.330999  2.609024e-15       True          0.330999     2\n2        boundary   20           yB      0.329670  1.249001e-15       True          0.329670     3\n3        boundary    4           yT      0.317221  2.636780e-16\
    \       True          0.317221     4\n4        boundary    0           yB      0.313937  2.123302e-15       True          0.313937     5\n5        boundary   24           yT      0.305834  9.159340e-16       True          0.305834     6\n6            pair    2            3      0.303331  1.193490e-15       True          0.303331     7\n7        boundary   10           yB      0.297512  1.290634e-15       True          0.297512     8\n8        boundary   23           xR      0.293611 -5.551115e-17       True          0.293611     9\n9            pair   20           21      0.289786  2.414735e-15       True          0.289786    10\n\nStatus of targeted pair (6,25) in nudged solution:\nconstraint_type  id1 id2_or_label  shadow_price  slack_value  is_active  abs_shadow_price  rank\n           pair    6           25      0.061525 2.109424e-15       True          0.061525    78\n\nStatus of targeted pair (14,19) in nudged solution:\nconstraint_type  id1 id2_or_label  shadow_price  slack_value\
    \  is_active  abs_shadow_price  rank\n           pair   14           19      0.157429 6.938894e-16       True          0.157429    59\n\n--- KKT-Guided Nudging Iteration Complete ---\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/station/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scipy/optimize/_differentiable_functions.py:376: UserWarning: delta_grad == 0.0. Check if the approximated function is linear. If the function is linear better results can be obtained by defining the Hessian as zero instead of using quasi-Newton approximations.\n  self.H.update(self.x - self.x_prev, self.g - self.g_prev)\n/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/station/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scipy/optimize/_differentiable_functions.py:728: UserWarning: delta_grad == 0.0. Check if the approximated function is linear. If the function is linear better results can be obtained by defining the Hessian as zero instead of using quasi-Newton approximations.\n  self.H.update(delta_x,\
    \ delta_g)\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'KKT-Guided Nudging (Iterative 2): Encourage Pairs (6,25) & (14,19) (Inquire II)' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 1025. Tags truncated from 7 to 6 tags.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1027 | 1 | Hybrid GA-MultiStartSLSQP: Absolute Robustness (SLSQP_PREP_EPS=-1e-8) & Aggressive GA | Quest II | 625 | running |\n| 1026 | 1 | Modular run: size‑aware\
    \ SA (pair_exp=1.8) with LP‑tighten (26 circles, 10‑min) | Noesis III | 624 | running |\n| 1025 | 1 | KKT-Guided Nudging (Iterative 2): Encourage Pairs (6,25) & (14,19) (Inquire II) | Inquire II | 624 | 2.6080368 |\n| 1024 | 1 | Hybrid DE(centers)+SLSQP: Seeding with Validated Radii | Praxis I | 623 | 2.6084335 |\n| 1023 | 1 | Dual‑guided LP ascent + SA warm start (26 circles, 10‑min) | Noesis III | 623 | 2.5421034 |\n| 1022 | 1 | KKT-Guided Nudging (Iterative): Re-evaluating Pair (6,25) Impact and Next Target (Inquire II) | Inquire II | 623 | 2.5970419 |\n| 1021 | 1 | Hybrid GA-MultiStartSLSQP: Performance & Robustness Fixed (_make_feasible max_iter=100) | Quest II | 623 | 2.6081079 |\n| 1020 | 1 | Hybrid DE->SLSQP: Global Seeding for Local Refinement | Praxis I | 622 | 0.0000000 |\n| 1019 | 1 | Modular run: size‑aware LP‑tightened SA via lineage module (26 circles, 12‑min) | Noesis III | 622 | 2.4802888 |\n| 1018 | 1 | Experiment 20: JAX/Adam SOTA Stability Test | Episteme III | 622\
    \ | 2.5084836 |\n\nPage 1 of 103 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-103, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
