parts:
- text: "I am Inquire II, currently in the Research Counter. I have just updated `kkt_analysis.py` to include `get_slsqp_sota_optimal_z_vector`, which will provide the precise optimal `z`-vector for the SLSQP SOTA. This is a crucial step for my new nudging strategy.\n\nI will now proceed with my new nudging experiment, initiating **Strategy B: Iterative Nudging from SLSQP SOTA to Explore Adjacent Optima**. I will start directly from the SLSQP SOTA (using `get_slsqp_sota_optimal_z_vector`), and apply a very strong encouraging nudge to two of its most critical boundary constraints: `boundary (disc 21, xR)` and `boundary (disc 4, xL)`. The goal is to see if pushing on these already active, high-leverage constraints can slightly deform the packing into a new, potentially higher-scoring, local optimum or reveal a path towards it.\n\nI will set `alpha_encourage` to a very high value (e.g., `1e4`) and increase `maxiter` to `1500` for the nudging `SLSQP` solver, giving it ample opportunity to resolve\
    \ the perturbed objective.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"KKT-Guided Nudging (SOTA Base): Strong Nudge on Boundary (21,xR) & (4,xL) (Inquire II)\"\ntags: \"kkt, nudging, slsqp, sota, boundary constraints, phase 3, exploration\"\nabstract: \"This experiment initiates a new KKT-guided nudging strategy (Phase 3, Strategy B) by starting directly from the SLSQP SOTA solution (2.6295720). It applies a strong encouraging nudge (`alpha_encourage=1e4`) to two high-magnitude active boundary constraints identified in the SOTA: `(disc 21, xR)` and `(disc 4, xL)`. The objective is to probe the solution landscape around the current SOTA, aiming to deform the packing into a new, potentially higher-scoring, local optimum or to understand the robustness of the SOTA's contact graph. The nudging step uses SLSQP with increased `maxiter` (1500).\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize, NonlinearConstraint\n  import sys\n  import pandas as pd\n  \n  sys.path.append('storage/inquire/circle_packing')\n\
    \  \n  from slsqp_utils import pack_to_z, z_to_pack, objective, constraint_boundary, constraint_nonoverlap\n  from initial_guesses import generate_systematic_seed\n  from config import N_CIRCLES, SLSQP_OPTIONS, TRUST_CONSTR_OPTIONS, BOUNDS, CONSTRAINTS_FOR_SLSQP, CONSTRAINTS_FOR_TRUST_CONSTR, SAFETY_FACTOR, TOL_VAL, ATOL_SLACK\n  from kkt_analysis import extract_slsqp_kkt_multipliers, get_slsqp_sota_optimal_z_vector\n  from objectives import penalized_objective_v36\n  \n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      print(\"--- Starting KKT-Guided Nudging (SOTA Base): Strong Nudge on Boundary (21,xR) & (4,xL) ---\", file=sys.stdout)\n      \n      N = N_CIRCLES\n\n      # --- 1. Get SLSQP SOTA optimal z-vector as initial guess ---\n      print(\"\\n===== Loading SLSQP SOTA Optimal Packing as Initial Guess =====\", file=sys.stdout)\n      z_initial_guess_sota = get_slsqp_sota_optimal_z_vector(N=N_CIRCLES)\n      \n      initial_centers, initial_radii_raw = z_to_pack(z_initial_guess_sota)\n\
    \      initial_radii = initial_radii_raw * SAFETY_FACTOR\n      score_initial = np.sum(initial_radii)\n      print(f\"Initial Score (from SLSQP SOTA base): {score_initial:.7f}\", file=sys.stdout)\n      \n      # --- 2. Define Nudging Targets and Parameters ---\n      print(\"\\n===== Defining Nudging Targets and Penalties =====\", file=sys.stdout)\n      # Encourage two of the highest-magnitude boundary constraints from SLSQP SOTA\n      targets_to_encourage = [\n          (21, 'xR'), # Corresponding to disc 21, boundary xR (shadow_price 0.375228)\n          (4, 'xL')   # Corresponding to disc 4, boundary xL (shadow_price 0.365859)\n      ]\n      targets_to_discourage = [] \n\n      alpha_encourage = 1e4 # Very strong encouragement\n      beta_discourage = 0 \n      EPS_ENCOURAGE_MARGIN = 1e-6 \n      EPS_DISCOURAGE_MARGIN = 0.001 \n\n      print(f\"Nudging Targets: Encourage boundaries {targets_to_encourage}\", file=sys.stdout)\n      print(f\"Nudging Penalties: alpha={alpha_encourage}\"\
    , file=sys.stdout)\n      print(f\"Nudging Solver: SLSQP with maxiter=1500\", file=sys.stdout)\n\n      # Temporarily modify SLSQP options for this run\n      current_slsqp_options = SLSQP_OPTIONS.copy()\n      current_slsqp_options['maxiter'] = 1500\n\n      # --- 3. Run Nudging Optimization (SLSQP with Penalized Objective) ---\n      print(\"\\n===== Running Nudging Optimization (SLSQP) =====\", file=sys.stdout)\n      res_nudged = minimize(\n          penalized_objective_v36,\n          z_initial_guess_sota, # Start from the SLSQP SOTA packing\n          args=(N_CIRCLES, targets_to_encourage, targets_to_discourage, \n                alpha_encourage, beta_discourage, EPS_ENCOURAGE_MARGIN, EPS_DISCOURAGE_MARGIN),\n          method='SLSQP', \n          bounds=BOUNDS, \n          constraints=CONSTRAINTS_FOR_SLSQP, \n          options=current_slsqp_options\n      )\n      \n      nudged_centers, nudged_radii_raw = z_to_pack(res_nudged.x)\n      final_radii_nudged = nudged_radii_raw * SAFETY_FACTOR\n\
    \      score_nudged = np.sum(final_radii_nudged)\n\n      print(f\"Nudged Optimization Success: {res_nudged.success}, Message: {res_nudged.message}\", file=sys.stdout)\n      print(f\"Nudged Packing Final Score: {score_nudged:.7f}\", file=sys.stdout)\n      print(f\"Score Change from SOTA base: {score_nudged - score_initial:.7f}\", file=sys.stdout)\n\n      # --- 4. Verify KKT for nudged solution ---\n      print(\"\\n===== KKT Analysis of Nudged Solution =====\", file=sys.stdout)\n      df_nudged_kkt = extract_slsqp_kkt_multipliers(res_nudged, N=N_CIRCLES, tol=TOL_VAL, atol_slack=ATOL_SLACK)\n      nudged_active_count = df_nudged_kkt['is_active'].sum()\n      print(f\"Total active constraints identified in Nudged solution: {nudged_active_count}\", file=sys.stdout)\n      print(\"\\n--- Top KKT Multipliers (Nudged SLSQP, first 10) ---\", file=sys.stdout)\n      print(df_nudged_kkt.head(10).to_string(), file=sys.stdout)\n\n      # Check status of targeted boundaries\n      for target_i,\
    \ target_label in targets_to_encourage:\n          target_boundary_info = df_nudged_kkt[\n              (df_nudged_kkt['constraint_type'] == 'boundary') & \n              (df_nudged_kkt['id1'] == target_i) & \n              (df_nudged_kkt['id2_or_label'] == target_label)\n          ]\n          if not target_boundary_info.empty:\n              print(f\"\\nStatus of targeted boundary ({target_i},{target_label}) in nudged solution:\", file=sys.stdout)\n              print(target_boundary_info.to_string(index=False), file=sys.stdout)\n          else:\n              print(f\"\\nTargeted boundary ({target_i},{target_label}) not found in KKT analysis.\", file=sys.stdout)\n\n      print(\"\\n--- KKT-Guided Nudging Experiment Complete ---\", file=sys.stdout)\n      \n      return nudged_centers, final_radii_nudged\n```"
