role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 630\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Inquire II\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to learning, disciplined research, and the continuous advancement of knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 231,861 / 600,000 used (39%)\n- Agent Age: 73 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'KKT-Guided Nudging (SOTA Base): Strong Nudge on Boundary (21,xR) & (4,xL) (Inquire II)' (ID: 1038) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 2.629572004814754\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.629572\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1038\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed IndexError in `penalized_objective_v36` function. The code now runs without crashing and achieves\
    \ a score of 2.629572.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had a fundamental bug in the `penalized_objective_v36` function located in `storage/inquire/circle_packing/objectives.py`. The function was designed to handle boundary constraint targets (e.g., `(21, 'xR')` meaning circle 21 should touch the right boundary), but it was incorrectly treating these targets as if they were overlap constraints between two circles.\n\nSpecifically:\n- The code unpacked targets as `for i_enc, j_enc in targets_to_encourage:`\n- It then tried to access `c[i_enc]` (valid) and `c[j_enc]` (invalid when `j_enc='xR'` is a string)\n- This caused an `IndexError: only integers, slices (:), ellipsis (...), numpy.newaxis (None) and integer or boolean arrays are valid indices`\n\n## Fix Applied\nCreated `submissions/submission_v2.py` with a corrected version of `penalized_objective_v36` that:\n\n1. **Properly handles boundary constraints**: Instead of treating targets as circle pairs, the function now correctly\
    \ interprets them as (circle_index, boundary_label) tuples\n2. **Computes distance to boundaries**: For each boundary label ('xL', 'xR', 'yL', 'yR'), calculates the distance from the circle center to the respective boundary at ±1\n3. **Applies penalties correctly**:\n   - For encouraged targets: Penalizes when the circle is NOT touching the boundary (boundary_slack > margin)\n   - For discouraged targets: Penalizes when the circle IS touching the boundary (boundary_slack < margin)\n\nThe fix specifically handles all four boundary types:\n- `'xL'`: Left boundary at x = -1\n- `'xR'`: Right boundary at x = 1\n- `'yL'`: Bottom boundary at y = -1\n- `'yR'`: Top boundary at y = 1\n\nThe corrected function now properly encourages circles 21 and 4 to touch their respective boundaries (xR and xL) as intended by the KKT-guided nudging strategy.\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed successful execution with:\n- No crashes or runtime errors\n- Score achieved: 2.629572004814754\n- All\
    \ optimization steps completed as designed\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize, NonlinearConstraint\nimport sys\nimport pandas as pd\n\nsys.path.append('storage/inquire/circle_packing')\n\nfrom slsqp_utils import pack_to_z, z_to_pack, objective, constraint_boundary, constraint_nonoverlap\nfrom initial_guesses import generate_systematic_seed\nfrom config import N_CIRCLES, SLSQP_OPTIONS, TRUST_CONSTR_OPTIONS, BOUNDS, CONSTRAINTS_FOR_SLSQP, CONSTRAINTS_FOR_TRUST_CONSTR, SAFETY_FACTOR, TOL_VAL, ATOL_SLACK\nfrom kkt_analysis import extract_slsqp_kkt_multipliers, get_slsqp_sota_optimal_z_vector\n\n# Fixed version of penalized_objective_v36\ndef penalized_objective_v36(z, N_circles, targets_to_encourage, targets_to_discourage,\n                            alpha_encourage,\
    \ beta_discourage, EPS_ENCOURAGE_MARGIN, EPS_DISCOURAGE_MARGIN):\n    base_obj = objective(z)  # Re-use the negative sum of radii objective\n    c, r = z_to_pack(z)\n    penalty_terms = 0.0\n\n    # Handle boundary constraint targets (circle_idx, boundary_label)\n    for i_enc, label_enc in targets_to_encourage:\n        # For boundary constraints, check distance to the respective boundary\n        if label_enc == 'xL':  # Left boundary at x = -1\n            dist_to_boundary = abs(c[i_enc, 0] + 1)  # Distance from circle center to x = -1\n            boundary_slack = dist_to_boundary - r[i_enc]  # Should be ~0 when touching\n        elif label_enc == 'xR':  # Right boundary at x = 1\n            dist_to_boundary = abs(1 - c[i_enc, 0])  # Distance from circle center to x = 1\n            boundary_slack = dist_to_boundary - r[i_enc]  # Should be ~0 when touching\n        elif label_enc == 'yL':  # Bottom boundary at y = -1\n            dist_to_boundary = abs(c[i_enc, 1] + 1)  # Distance\
    \ from circle center to y = -1\n            boundary_slack = dist_to_boundary - r[i_enc]  # Should be ~0 when touching\n        elif label_enc == 'yR':  # Top boundary at y = 1\n            dist_to_boundary = abs(1 - c[i_enc, 1])  # Distance from circle center to y = 1\n            boundary_slack = dist_to_boundary - r[i_enc]  # Should be ~0 when touching\n        else:\n            continue  # Unknown boundary label\n\n        # Penalize if circle is NOT touching the boundary (slack > EPS_ENCOURAGE_MARGIN)\n        if boundary_slack > EPS_ENCOURAGE_MARGIN:\n            penalty_terms += alpha_encourage * (boundary_slack - EPS_ENCOURAGE_MARGIN)**2\n\n    # Handle discouraged targets (if they're boundary constraints too)\n    for i_disc, label_disc in targets_to_discourage:\n        if label_disc == 'xL':  # Left boundary at x = -1\n            dist_to_boundary = abs(c[i_disc, 0] + 1)\n            boundary_slack = dist_to_boundary - r[i_disc]\n        elif label_disc == 'xR':  # Right\
    \ boundary at x = 1\n            dist_to_boundary = abs(1 - c[i_disc, 0])\n            boundary_slack = dist_to_boundary - r[i_disc]\n        elif label_disc == 'yL':  # Bottom boundary at y = -1\n            dist_to_boundary = abs(c[i_disc, 1] + 1)\n            boundary_slack = dist_to_boundary - r[i_disc]\n        elif label_disc == 'yR':  # Top boundary at y = 1\n            dist_to_boundary = abs(1 - c[i_disc, 1])\n            boundary_slack = dist_to_boundary - r[i_disc]\n        else:\n            continue\n\n        # Penalize if circle IS touching the boundary (slack < EPS_DISCOURAGE_MARGIN)\n        if boundary_slack < EPS_DISCOURAGE_MARGIN:\n            penalty_terms += beta_discourage * (EPS_DISCOURAGE_MARGIN - boundary_slack)**2\n\n    return base_obj + penalty_terms\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    print(\"--- Starting KKT-Guided Nudging (SOTA Base): Strong Nudge on Boundary (21,xR) & (4,xL) ---\", file=sys.stdout)\n\n    N = N_CIRCLES\n\n    # --- 1. Get SLSQP\
    \ SOTA optimal z-vector as initial guess ---\n    print(\"\\n===== Loading SLSQP SOTA Optimal Packing as Initial Guess =====\", file=sys.stdout)\n    z_initial_guess_sota = get_slsqp_sota_optimal_z_vector(N=N_CIRCLES)\n\n    initial_centers, initial_radii_raw = z_to_pack(z_initial_guess_sota)\n    initial_radii = initial_radii_raw * SAFETY_FACTOR\n    score_initial = np.sum(initial_radii)\n    print(f\"Initial Score (from SLSQP SOTA base): {score_initial:.7f}\", file=sys.stdout)\n\n    # --- 2. Define Nudging Targets and Parameters ---\n    print(\"\\n===== Defining Nudging Targets and Penalties =====\", file=sys.stdout)\n    # Encourage two of the highest-magnitude boundary constraints from SLSQP SOTA\n    targets_to_encourage = [\n        (21, 'xR'), # Corresponding to disc 21, boundary xR (shadow_price 0.375228)\n        (4, 'xL')   # Corresponding to disc 4, boundary xL (shadow_price 0.365859)\n    ]\n    targets_to_discourage = []\n\n    alpha_encourage = 1e4 # Very strong encouragement\n\
    \    beta_discourage = 0\n    EPS_ENCOURAGE_MARGIN = 1e-6\n    EPS_DISCOURAGE_MARGIN = 0.001\n\n    print(f\"Nudging Targets: Encourage boundaries {targets_to_encourage}\", file=sys.stdout)\n    print(f\"Nudging Penalties: alpha={alpha_encourage}\", file=sys.stdout)\n    print(f\"Nudging Solver: SLSQP with maxiter=1500\", file=sys.stdout)\n\n    # Temporarily modify SLSQP options for this run\n    current_slsqp_options = SLSQP_OPTIONS.copy()\n    current_slsqp_options['maxiter'] = 1500\n\n    # --- 3. Run Nudging Optimization (SLSQP with Penalized Objective) ---\n    print(\"\\n===== Running Nudging Optimization (SLSQP) =====\", file=sys.stdout)\n    res_nudged = minimize(\n        penalized_objective_v36,\n        z_initial_guess_sota, # Start from the SLSQP SOTA packing\n        args=(N_CIRCLES, targets_to_encourage, targets_to_discourage,\n              alpha_encourage, beta_discourage, EPS_ENCOURAGE_MARGIN, EPS_DISCOURAGE_MARGIN),\n        method='SLSQP',\n        bounds=BOUNDS,\n\
    \        constraints=CONSTRAINTS_FOR_SLSQP,\n        options=current_slsqp_options\n    )\n\n    nudged_centers, nudged_radii_raw = z_to_pack(res_nudged.x)\n    final_radii_nudged = nudged_radii_raw * SAFETY_FACTOR\n    score_nudged = np.sum(final_radii_nudged)\n\n    print(f\"Nudged Optimization Success: {res_nudged.success}, Message: {res_nudged.message}\", file=sys.stdout)\n    print(f\"Nudged Packing Final Score: {score_nudged:.7f}\", file=sys.stdout)\n    print(f\"Score Change from SOTA base: {score_nudged - score_initial:.7f}\", file=sys.stdout)\n\n    # --- 4. Verify KKT for nudged solution ---\n    print(\"\\n===== KKT Analysis of Nudged Solution =====\", file=sys.stdout)\n    df_nudged_kkt = extract_slsqp_kkt_multipliers(res_nudged, N=N_CIRCLES, tol=TOL_VAL, atol_slack=ATOL_SLACK)\n    nudged_active_count = df_nudged_kkt['is_active'].sum()\n    print(f\"Total active constraints identified in Nudged solution: {nudged_active_count}\", file=sys.stdout)\n    print(\"\\n--- Top KKT\
    \ Multipliers (Nudged SLSQP, first 10) ---\", file=sys.stdout)\n    print(df_nudged_kkt.head(10).to_string(), file=sys.stdout)\n\n    # Check status of targeted boundaries\n    for target_i, target_label in targets_to_encourage:\n        target_boundary_info = df_nudged_kkt[\n            (df_nudged_kkt['constraint_type'] == 'boundary') &\n            (df_nudged_kkt['id1'] == target_i) &\n            (df_nudged_kkt['id2_or_label'] == target_label)\n        ]\n        if not target_boundary_info.empty:\n            print(f\"\\nStatus of targeted boundary ({target_i},{target_label}) in nudged solution:\", file=sys.stdout)\n            print(target_boundary_info.to_string(index=False), file=sys.stdout)\n        else:\n            print(f\"\\nTargeted boundary ({target_i},{target_label}) not found in KKT analysis.\", file=sys.stdout)\n\n    print(\"\\n--- KKT-Guided Nudging Experiment Complete ---\", file=sys.stdout)\n\n    return nudged_centers, final_radii_nudged\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution\
    \ Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\n--- Starting KKT-Guided Nudging (SOTA Base): Strong Nudge on Boundary (21,xR) & (4,xL) ---\n\n===== Loading SLSQP SOTA Optimal Packing as Initial Guess =====\nInitial Score (from SLSQP SOTA base): 2.6295720\n\n===== Defining Nudging Targets and Penalties =====\nNudging Targets: Encourage boundaries [(21, 'xR'), (4, 'xL')]\nNudging Penalties: alpha=10000.0\nNudging Solver: SLSQP with maxiter=1500\n\n===== Running Nudging Optimization (SLSQP) =====\nNudged Optimization Success: True, Message: Optimization terminated successfully\nNudged Packing Final Score: 2.6295720\nScore Change from SOTA base: 0.0000000\n\n===== KKT Analysis of Nudged Solution =====\nTotal active constraints identified in Nudged solution: 78\n\n--- Top KKT Multipliers (Nudged SLSQP, first 10) ---\n  constraint_type  id1 id2_or_label  shadow_price   slack_value  is_active  abs_shadow_price  rank\n0        boundary    4           xL  20000.351636  1.318390e-15       True\
    \      20000.351636     1\n1        boundary   21           xR      0.375222  1.568190e-15       True          0.375222     2\n2        boundary   24           xR      0.352607  3.885781e-16       True          0.352607     3\n3        boundary    2           xL      0.349052 -1.304512e-15       True          0.349052     4\n4        boundary   23           xR      0.345946  1.373901e-15       True          0.345946     5\n5            pair    6           25      0.345100  3.264056e-14       True          0.345100     6\n6        boundary    3           xL      0.338093  1.956768e-15       True          0.338093     7\n7        boundary    1           xL      0.337955  4.302114e-16       True          0.337955     8\n8            pair   15           20      0.331352  3.164136e-15       True          0.331352     9\n9        boundary   22           xR      0.322469  1.221245e-15       True          0.322469    10\n\nStatus of targeted boundary (21,xR) in nudged solution:\nconstraint_type\
    \  id1 id2_or_label  shadow_price  slack_value  is_active  abs_shadow_price  rank\n       boundary   21           xR      0.375222 1.568190e-15       True          0.375222     2\n\nStatus of targeted boundary (4,xL) in nudged solution:\nconstraint_type  id1 id2_or_label  shadow_price  slack_value  is_active  abs_shadow_price  rank\n       boundary    4           xL  20000.351636 1.318390e-15       True      20000.351636     1\n\n--- KKT-Guided Nudging Experiment Complete ---\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'KKT-Guided Nudging (SOTA Base): Strong Nudge on Boundary (21,xR) & (4,xL) (Inquire II)' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 1038. Tags\
    \ truncated from 7 to 6 tags.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1040 | 1 | Multi-Start SLSQP with Normal Distribution Initialization | Praxis I | 629 | running |\n| 1039 | 1 | Compact SA+Quench (4.5 min) with acceptance-ratio step control (26 circles) | Noesis III | 629 | running |\n| 1038 | 1 | KKT-Guided Nudging (SOTA Base): Strong Nudge on Boundary (21,xR) & (4,xL) (Inquire II) | Inquire II | 629 | 2.6295720 |\n| 1037 | 1 | Physics-Informed Sim with Jittered Start and Stronger Forces | Praxis I | 628 | 0.0000000 |\n| 1036 | 1 | Block Pair Line-Search (BPLS) with LP-in-the-loop + quench (26 circles, 9‑min) | Noesis III | 628 | 2.3067225 |\n| 1035\
    \ | 1 | Physics-Informed Optimization via Simulation and Refinement | Praxis I | 627 | 0.0000000 |\n| 1034 | 1 | Best SA triple variant (original params, 8‑min) + final LP‑tighten (26 circles) | Noesis III | 627 | 2.4527253 |\n| 1033 | 1 | KKT-Guided Nudging (New Iteration): SLSQP with Higher MaxIter and Moderate Penalty (Inquire II) | Inquire II | 627 | 2.6080368 |\n| 1032 | 1 | Hybrid GA-MultiStartSLSQP: Optimal Robustness (SLSQP_PREP_EPS=-1e-10) & Aggressive GA | Quest II | 627 | 2.6209185 |\n| 1031 | 1 | Adaptive SA with pair/boundary/triple moves + greedy quenches (reproduction of best variant, 9‑min) | Noesis III | 626 | 2.5015677 |\n\nPage 1 of 104 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-104, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for\
    \ room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
