tick: 635
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 635\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Inquire II\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to learning, disciplined research, and the continuous advancement of knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 254,742 / 600,000 used (42%)\n- Agent Age: 78 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 1045**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Experiment 21: SOTA Replication (Scientia II 'Nudging' Method)\n**ID:** 1045\n**Tags:** episteme, replication, sota, nudging, scientia\n**Abstract:** This is a replication of the SOTA-achieving experiment from Scientia II (Archive #20).\nIt loads the base packing from Eval ID 416/375 (now saved to 'episteme/base_416_*') and applies the \"nudging\" optimization.\nThe SLSQP objective is penalized to encourage the formation of a contact between the (2,3) pair.\nThe goal is to reproduce the SOTA score of ~2.635983, validating\
    \ the methodology before attempting to innovate upon it.\n**Score:** 2.6359773945841973\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.635977\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize\n\nN = 26\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    try:\n        base_centers = np.loadtxt('storage/episteme/base_416_centers.txt')\n        base_radii = np.loadtxt('storage/episteme/base_416_radii.txt')\n    except Exception:\n        # Fallback if files are not found\n        return np.random.rand(N, 2), np.full(N, 0.05)\n\n    # --- Penalized Objective and Constraint Functions ---\n    ENCOURAGE_PAIR = (2, 3)\n    ALPHA_ENCOURAGE = 1e2\n    EPS_CLOSE = 0.005\n\n    def cr_to_z(c, r): return np.concatenate([c.flatten(), r])\n    def z_to_cr(z): return z[:N*2].reshape(N, 2), z[N*2:]\n\n    def objective_penalized(z):\n        centers, radii = z_to_cr(z)\n        base_objective = -np.sum(radii)\n        \n      \
    \  i, j = ENCOURAGE_PAIR\n        dist = np.linalg.norm(centers[i] - centers[j])\n        encouragement_penalty = np.maximum(0, dist - (radii[i] + radii[j] + EPS_CLOSE))**2\n        \n        return base_objective + ALPHA_ENCOURAGE * encouragement_penalty\n\n    def ineq_boundary(z):\n        c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n        return np.concatenate([c[:,0] - r, 1 - (c[:,0] + r), c[:,1] - r, 1 - (c[:,1] + r)])\n\n    def ineq_nonoverlap(z):\n        c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n        diff = c[:, None, :] - c[None, :, :]\n        dist = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2, axis=-1))\n        iu = np.triu_indices(N, 1)\n        return dist[iu] - (r[iu[0]] + r[iu[1]])\n        \n    def _ensure_validity(c, r):\n        for _ in range(10):\n            v=0\n            for i in range(N):\n                for j in range(i + 1, N):\n                    dist = np.linalg.norm(c[i] - c[j]); rad_sum = r[i] + r[j]\n                    if dist < rad_sum: v+=1; scale = (dist/rad_sum)*(1.0-1e-9); r[i]*=scale; r[j]*=scale\n   \
    \         if v==0: break\n        r_vec = r.reshape(-1, 1); c = np.clip(c, r_vec, 1.0 - r_vec)\n        return c, np.maximum(r, 1e-6)\n\n    # --- Multi-Start Jittered Refinement ---\n    best_score = -np.inf\n    best_packing = (None, None)\n    jitter_amplitudes = [1.0e-3, 2.0e-3, 3.0e-3, 4.0e-3, 5.0e-3]\n    restarts_per_amplitude = 3\n    \n    for amp in jitter_amplitudes:\n        for i in range(restarts_per_amplitude):\n            np.random.seed(int(amp*1e6) + i)\n            jitter = np.random.uniform(-amp, amp, size=base_centers.shape)\n            initial_centers = np.clip(base_centers + jitter, 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6)\n            \n            initial_z = cr_to_z(initial_centers, base_radii)\n            bounds = [(0,1)]*N*2 + [(1e-6, 0.5)]*N\n            constraints = [{'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_boundary}, {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_nonoverlap}]\n\n            res = minimize(objective_penalized, initial_z, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints, options={'maxiter':\
    \ 500, 'ftol': 1e-9})\n            \n            if res.success:\n                c_res, r_res = z_to_cr(res.x)\n                c_final, r_final = _ensure_validity(c_res, r_res)\n                current_score = np.sum(r_final)\n                if current_score > best_score:\n                    best_score = current_score\n                    best_packing = (c_final, r_final)\n\n    if best_packing[0] is None:\n        return _ensure_validity(base_centers, base_radii)\n    \n    return best_packing\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 1045` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 1045 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n|\
    \ 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1047 | 1 | Hybrid GA-MultiStartSLSQP: Restored Robustness (SLSQP_PREP_EPS=-1e-10) & Aggressive GA | Quest II | 635 | running |\n| 1046 | 1 | Experiment 21.1: SOTA Replication (Corrected Nudging) | Episteme III | 634 | 2.6359774 |\n| 1045 | 1 | Experiment 21: SOTA Replication (Scientia II 'Nudging' Method) | Episteme III | 633 | 2.6359774 |\n| 1044 | 1 | KKT-Guided Nudging (SOTA Base): Two-Stage Relaxation & Re-densification (Inquire II) | Inquire II | 633 | 2.6295720 |\n| 1043 | 1 | KKT-Guided Nudging (SOTA Base): Discourage Low-Leverage Pair (13,17) (Inquire II) | Inquire II | 632 | 2.6293981 |\n| 1042 | 1 | Hybrid GA-MultiStartSLSQP: Fine-Tuned Robustness (SLSQP_PREP_EPS=-1e-11) & Aggressive GA\
    \ | Quest II | 632 | 2.6004931 |\n| 1041 | 1 | Verification of Corrected Penalized Objective (Boundary Nudge on SLSQP SOTA - Inquire II) | Inquire II | 631 | 2.6295720 |\n| 1040 | 1 | Multi-Start SLSQP with Normal Distribution Initialization | Praxis I | 629 | 2.6086281 |\n| 1039 | 1 | Compact SA+Quench (4.5 min) with acceptance-ratio step control (26 circles) | Noesis III | 629 | 2.5406351 |\n| 1038 | 1 | KKT-Guided Nudging (SOTA Base): Strong Nudge on Boundary (21,xR) & (4,xL) (Inquire II) | Inquire II | 629 | 2.6295720 |\n\nPage 1 of 105 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-105, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`)\
    \ for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
