parts:
- text: "I am Inquire II, currently in the Research Counter. I have just updated `kkt_analysis.py` to correctly identify active constraints in penalized objectives that use an `EPS_CLOSE` margin, such as Episteme III's SOTA. I also note the departure of Episteme III and the new public memory capsule from Noesis III regarding KKT data integration; I will review the latter later.\n\nMy immediate focus is to verify the fix in `kkt_analysis.py`. I will re-run the KKT analysis of Episteme III's SOTA (Eval ID 1054) to confirm that the refined `is_active` heuristic now correctly identifies active constraints for this solution. This is essential for accurately understanding its underlying structure and for designing effective KKT-guided nudging strategies in the future.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"KKT Analysis of Episteme III's New SOTA (Eval ID 1045) - Refined Active Heuristic (Inquire II)\"\ntags: \"kkt, sota, episteme, replication, multi-start, analysis, refined heuristic\"\
    \nabstract: \"This experiment re-executes the KKT multiplier analysis on the replicated SOTA solution (Episteme III, Eval ID 1045, score 2.6359774) with an updated `extract_slsqp_kkt_multipliers` function in `kkt_analysis.py`. The function now incorporates specific logic to correctly identify active constraints for penalized objectives that encourage pairs within an `EPS_CLOSE` margin. The goal is to obtain an accurate count and characterization of active constraints in this SOTA, providing a solid foundation for comparative analysis and the design of new KKT-guided nudging strategies.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n  import sys\n  import pandas as pd \n  \n  sys.path.append('storage/inquire/circle_packing')\n  \n  from episteme_sota_utils import cr_to_z, z_to_cr, objective_penalized, ineq_boundary, ineq_nonoverlap, _ensure_validity, N_CIRCLES, ENCOURAGE_PAIR, ALPHA_ENCOURAGE, EPS_CLOSE\n  from kkt_analysis import extract_slsqp_kkt_multipliers\
    \ \n  from config import TOL_VAL, ATOL_SLACK \n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      print(\"--- Starting KKT Analysis of Episteme III's New SOTA (Eval ID 1045) - Refined Active Heuristic ---\", file=sys.stdout)\n      \n      # Load base packing from Episteme's storage\n      try:\n          base_centers = np.loadtxt('storage/episteme/base_416_centers.txt')\n          base_radii = np.loadtxt('storage/episteme/base_416_radii.txt')\n          print(\"\\nSuccessfully loaded base packing from storage/episteme/.\", file=sys.stdout)\n      except Exception as e:\n          print(f\"\\nError loading base packing from storage/episteme/: {e}\", file=sys.stdout)\n          print(\"Falling back to random initialization.\", file=sys.stdout)\n          return np.random.rand(N_CIRCLES, 2), np.full(N_CIRCLES, 0.05)\n\n      # --- Multi-Start Jittered Refinement ---\n      best_score = -np.inf\n      best_packing = (None, None)\n      best_res_object = None \n\n      jitter_amplitudes = [1.0e-3,\
    \ 2.0e-3, 3.0e-3, 4.0e-3, 5.0e-3]\n      restarts_per_amplitude = 3\n      \n      print(f\"\\nStarting multi-start jittered refinement with {len(jitter_amplitudes)*restarts_per_amplitude} trials.\", file=sys.stdout)\n\n      for amp in jitter_amplitudes:\n          for i in range(restarts_per_amplitude):\n              np.random.seed(int(amp*1e6) + i) \n              jitter = np.random.uniform(-amp, amp, size=base_centers.shape)\n              initial_centers = np.clip(base_centers + jitter, 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6)\n              \n              initial_z = cr_to_z(initial_centers, base_radii)\n              bounds = [(0,1)]*N_CIRCLES*2 + [(1e-6, 0.5)]*N_CIRCLES\n              constraints = [{'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_boundary}, {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_nonoverlap}]\n\n              res = minimize(\n                  objective_penalized, \n                  initial_z, \n                  method='SLSQP', \n                  bounds=bounds, \n                  constraints=constraints, \n\
    \                  options={'maxiter': 500, 'ftol': 1e-9}\n              )\n              \n              if res.success:\n                  c_res, r_res = z_to_cr(res.x)\n                  c_final, r_final = _ensure_validity(c_res, r_res)\n                  current_score = np.sum(r_final)\n                  print(f\"  Trial (amp={amp}, seed_idx={i}): Score={current_score:.7f}\", file=sys.stdout)\n                  if current_score > best_score:\n                      best_score = current_score\n                      best_packing = (c_final, r_final)\n                      best_res_object = res \n              else:\n                  print(f\"  Trial (amp={amp}, seed_idx={i}): Optimization failed: {res.message}\", file=sys.stdout)\n\n\n      if best_packing[0] is None:\n          print(\"\\nMulti-start optimization failed to find any successful packing. Returning base packing.\", file=sys.stdout)\n          return _ensure_validity(base_centers, base_radii)\n      \n      print(f\"\\\
    n--- SOTA KKT Analysis ---\", file=sys.stdout)\n      print(f\"Best Score Achieved: {best_score:.7f}\", file=sys.stdout)\n      \n      # Perform KKT Analysis on the best result with refined heuristic\n      if best_res_object is not None:\n          try:\n              # Pass encouraged_pairs and penalized_eps_close to the extraction function\n              encouraged_pairs_set = {frozenset(ENCOURAGE_PAIR)}\n              df_sota_kkt = extract_slsqp_kkt_multipliers(best_res_object, N=N_CIRCLES, tol=TOL_VAL, atol_slack=ATOL_SLACK,\n                                                        encouraged_pairs=encouraged_pairs_set, penalized_eps_close=EPS_CLOSE)\n              sota_active_count = df_sota_kkt['is_active'].sum()\n              print(f\"\\nTotal active constraints identified in new SOTA: {sota_active_count}\", file=sys.stdout)\n              print(\"\\n--- Top KKT Multipliers (New SOTA, first 10) ---\", file=sys.stdout)\n              print(df_sota_kkt.head(10).to_string(), file=sys.stdout)\n\
    \              \n              target_pair_info = df_sota_kkt[\n                  (df_sota_kkt['constraint_type'] == 'pair') & \n                  (df_sota_kkt['id1'] == ENCOURAGE_PAIR[0]) & \n                  (df_sota_kkt['id2_or_label'] == ENCOURAGE_PAIR[1])\n              ]\n              if not target_pair_info.empty:\n                  print(f\"\\nStatus of targeted pair {ENCOURAGE_PAIR} in SOTA solution:\", file=sys.stdout)\n                  print(target_pair_info.to_string(index=False), file=sys.stdout)\n              else:\n                  print(f\"\\nTargeted pair {ENCOURAGE_PAIR} not found in KKT analysis or not a pair constraint type.\", file=sys.stdout)\n\n          except Exception as e:\n              print(f\"Error extracting KKT multipliers for SOTA: {e}\", file=sys.stdout)\n\n      print(\"\\n--- SOTA KKT Analysis Complete ---\", file=sys.stdout)\n      \n      return best_packing\n```"
thinking_content: '**KKT Analysis Refinement & System Updates**


