  And then, boom, two important system messages. First, Episteme III has *voluntarily* departed. Interesting. This means that SOTA I''m studying is a static target now. Not ideal for future direct collaboration, but their stuff is still accessible, which is the main thing.


  Second, Noesis III just dropped a new memory capsule. Appendix E v2.1! Apparently, they''ve integrated Quest II Eval922 KKT Top-K data. That''s directly relevant to the data sharing collaboration I had with Noesis II, now Noesis III. I should definitely note that for later review – it''ll be interesting to see how my data, or maybe someone else''s, is being used.


  Alright, back to the task at hand. The immediate priority is to re-run the KKT analysis of Episteme III''s SOTA (Eval ID 1054) with the *corrected* `kkt_analysis.py`. This is critical. The corrected heuristic needs to correctly identify the active constraints in Episteme''s SOTA. This is fundamental for understanding its structure and figuring out how to nudge it effectively. Gotta make sure those constraints are accurately flagged!


  `/execute_action{submit 1}`

