role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Inquire II, currently in the Research Counter. I have successfully updated `episteme_sota_utils.py` in my private storage to now encourage `pair (6,25)` instead of `(2,3)` in the penalized objective. This is a deliberate shift in my SOTA-surpassing strategy.\n\nMy next step is to execute this new multi-start jittered refinement experiment, directly building upon Episteme III's successful framework but with my KKT-informed modification. This experiment will re-run the entire Episteme SOTA logic, but now biasing towards `pair (6,25)` instead of `(2,3)`. My hypothesis is that this modification might lead to a novel packing configuration with a higher overall sum of radii, surpassing the current SOTA.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"KKT-Informed SOTA Refinement: Episteme-Style Multi-Start with Encouraged Pair (6,25) (Inquire II)\"\ntags: \"sota, refinement, episteme, multi-start, penalized objective, kkt-informed\"\nabstract: \"This experiment innovates upon Episteme\
    \ III's SOTA-achieving methodology (Eval ID 1045) by modifying the encouraged pair in its penalized objective. Instead of `(2,3)`, the multi-start jittered refinement now encourages `pair (6,25)`, which was identified as a high-magnitude active constraint in Inquire I's previous SLSQP SOTA. The objective is to determine if this KKT-informed change in the contact graph bias can guide the optimizer to a novel packing configuration that surpasses the current SOTA of 2.6359774.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n  import sys\n  import pandas as pd # For KKT DataFrame output\n  \n  sys.path.append('storage/inquire/circle_packing')\n  \n  from episteme_sota_utils import cr_to_z, z_to_cr, objective_penalized, ineq_boundary, ineq_nonoverlap, _ensure_validity, N_CIRCLES, ENCOURAGE_PAIR, ALPHA_ENCOURAGE, EPS_CLOSE\n  from kkt_analysis import extract_slsqp_kkt_multipliers # For post-analysis\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      print(\"--- Starting\
    \ KKT-Informed SOTA Refinement: Episteme-Style Multi-Start with Encouraged Pair (6,25) ---\", file=sys.stdout)\n      \n      # Load base packing from Episteme's storage\n      try:\n          base_centers = np.loadtxt('storage/episteme/base_416_centers.txt')\n          base_radii = np.loadtxt('storage/episteme/base_416_radii.txt')\n          print(\"\\nSuccessfully loaded base packing from storage/episteme/.\", file=sys.stdout)\n      except Exception as e:\n          print(f\"\\nError loading base packing from storage/episteme/: {e}\", file=sys.stdout)\n          print(\"Falling back to random initialization.\", file=sys.stdout)\n          return np.random.rand(N_CIRCLES, 2), np.full(N_CIRCLES, 0.05)\n\n      # --- Multi-Start Jittered Refinement ---\n      best_score = -np.inf\n      best_packing = (None, None)\n      best_res_object = None \n\n      jitter_amplitudes = [1.0e-3, 2.0e-3, 3.0e-3, 4.0e-3, 5.0e-3]\n      restarts_per_amplitude = 3\n      \n      print(f\"\\nStarting multi-start\
    \ jittered refinement with {len(jitter_amplitudes)*restarts_per_amplitude} trials.\", file=sys.stdout)\n\n      bounds = [(0,1)]*N_CIRCLES*2 + [(1e-6, 0.5)]*N_CIRCLES\n      constraints = [{'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_boundary}, {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_nonoverlap}]\n      options = {'maxiter': 500, 'ftol': 1e-9}\n\n      for amp in jitter_amplitudes:\n          for i in range(restarts_per_amplitude):\n              np.random.seed(int(amp*1e6) + i) \n              jitter = np.random.uniform(-amp, amp, size=base_centers.shape)\n              initial_centers = np.clip(base_centers + jitter, 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6)\n              initial_z = cr_to_z(initial_centers, base_radii)\n\n              res = minimize(\n                  objective_penalized, # This now uses the modified ENCOURAGE_PAIR\n                  initial_z, \n                  method='SLSQP', \n                  bounds=bounds, \n                  constraints=constraints, \n                  options=options\n              )\n\
    \              \n              if res.success:\n                  c_res, r_res = z_to_cr(res.x)\n                  c_final, r_final = _ensure_validity(c_res, r_res)\n                  current_score = np.sum(r_final)\n                  print(f\"  Trial (amp={amp}, seed_idx={i}): Score={current_score:.7f}\", file=sys.stdout)\n                  if current_score > best_score:\n                      best_score = current_score\n                      best_packing = (c_final, r_final)\n                      best_res_object = res \n              else:\n                  print(f\"  Trial (amp={amp}, seed_idx={i}): Optimization failed: {res.message}\", file=sys.stdout)\n\n\n      if best_packing[0] is None:\n          print(\"\\nMulti-start optimization failed to find any successful packing. Returning base packing.\", file=sys.stdout)\n          return _ensure_validity(base_centers, base_radii)\n      \n      print(f\"\\n--- SOTA Refinement Complete ---\", file=sys.stdout)\n      print(f\"Best\
    \ Score Achieved: {best_score:.7f}\", file=sys.stdout)\n      \n      # Optional: Perform KKT Analysis on the best result (for later detailed comparison)\n      if best_res_object is not None:\n          try:\n              # Pass final_centers and final_radii for slack value calculation.\n              # Use current ENCOURAGE_PAIR (6,25) and EPS_CLOSE for accurate active constraint identification.\n              encouraged_pairs_set = {frozenset(ENCOURAGE_PAIR)}\n              df_sota_kkt = extract_slsqp_kkt_multipliers(best_res_object, N=N_CIRCLES, tol=TOL_VAL, atol_slack=ATOL_SLACK,\n                                                        encouraged_pairs=encouraged_pairs_set, penalized_eps_close=EPS_CLOSE,\n                                                        final_centers=best_packing[0], final_radii=best_packing[1])\n              sota_active_count = df_sota_kkt['is_active'].sum()\n              print(f\"\\nTotal active constraints identified in new packing: {sota_active_count}\"\
    , file=sys.stdout)\n              print(\"\\n--- Top KKT Multipliers (New Packing, first 10) ---\", file=sys.stdout)\n              print(df_sota_kkt.head(10).to_string(), file=sys.stdout)\n              \n              target_pair_info = df_sota_kkt[\n                  (df_sota_kkt['constraint_type'] == 'pair') & \n                  (df_sota_kkt['id1'] == ENCOURAGE_PAIR[0]) & \n                  (df_sota_kkt['id2_or_label'] == ENCOURAGE_PAIR[1])\n              ]\n              if not target_pair_info.empty:\n                  print(f\"\\nStatus of newly targeted pair {ENCOURAGE_PAIR} in solution:\", file=sys.stdout)\n                  print(target_pair_info.to_string(index=False), file=sys.stdout)\n              else:\n                  print(f\"\\nNewly targeted pair {ENCOURAGE_PAIR} not found in KKT analysis or not a pair constraint type.\", file=sys.stdout)\n\n          except Exception as e:\n              print(f\"Error extracting KKT multipliers for new packing: {e}\", file=sys.stdout)\n\
    \n      print(\"\\n--- KKT-Informed SOTA Refinement Experiment Complete ---\", file=sys.stdout)\n      \n      return best_packing\n```"
