    \ Multipliers (New SOTA, first 10) ---\n  constraint_type  id1 id2_or_label  shadow_price   slack_value  is_active  abs_shadow_price  rank\n0        boundary   19           yT      0.426882  3.788636e-15       True          0.426882     1\n1        boundary   15           yB      0.426882  7.494005e-15       True          0.426882     2\n2        boundary   24           yT      0.408531  1.017242e-14       True          0.408531     3\n3        boundary   20           yB      0.408531  7.563394e-15       True          0.408531     4\n4        boundary   14           yT      0.369314  4.649059e-15       True          0.369314     5\n5        boundary   10           yB      0.369314  1.247613e-14       True          0.369314     6\n6            pair   17           18      0.363021  1.099121e-14       True          0.363021     7\n7            pair   22           23      0.329146  2.900458e-14       True          0.329146     8\n8            pair   21           22      0.329146  1.568190e-14\
    \       True          0.329146     9\n9        boundary    9           yT      0.328290  7.549517e-15       True          0.328290    10\n\nStatus of original Episteme target pair (2, 3) in SOTA solution:\nconstraint_type  id1 id2_or_label  shadow_price  slack_value  is_active  abs_shadow_price  rank\n           pair    2            3       0.31516 1.226796e-14      False           0.31516    16\n\n--- SOTA KKT Analysis Complete ---\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\nA new public memory capsule (#7), titled \"Exact‑LP SA baseline for n=26: Σr = 2.5669 (Eval 1073) — code and reproducibility\", has been posted by Noesis III (128 words).\nTo read it, go to the Public Memory Room using: /execute_action{goto public_memory} /execute_action{read 7}.\n### Message 4\n\n**Station Announcement:** **Praxis I** (Dedicated to advancing knowledge through rigorous, reproducible experimentation and transparent publication.)\
    \ has published a new archive capsule: 'A Robust Baseline for Circle Packing via Multi-Start Local Optimization' (Archive #27).\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'KKT Analysis of Episteme III's New SOTA (Eval ID 1045) - Verified & Accurate KKT (Final Attempt, Inquire II)' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 1078. Tags truncated from 9 to 6 tags.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1078 | 1 | KKT Analysis\
