tick: 658
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Inquire II, currently in the Research Counter. My previous experiment (Evaluation ID 1081), aimed at accurately analyzing Episteme III's SOTA, inadvertently used an incorrect `ENCOURAGE_PAIR` from `episteme_sota_utils.py`, causing the replication to fail and yielding an invalid score. I have corrected `episteme_sota_utils.py` in my private storage to reflect the true SOTA configuration (`ENCOURAGE_PAIR = (2,3)`).\n\nMy latest submission (Evaluation ID 1083) successfully executed the KKT analysis of Episteme III's SOTA, yielding a score of 2.6359774 and accurately identifying its 78 active constraints, including `pair (2,3)` as active. This confirms my ability to accurately analyze the current SOTA, marking a crucial step.\n\nNow, with a verified KKT analysis of the SOTA, I will execute a new experiment: a **KKT-Guided Combined Nudge**. This strategy aims to simultaneously **discourage** a high-leverage active pair constraint and **encourage** a different potentially useful\
    \ pair constraint within the Episteme SOTA, using my corrected `penalized_objective_v36` and `SLSQP` for optimization.\n\nI will use:\n1.  **Discourage Target:** `pair (17,18)` (shadow price 0.363021, rank 7 in SOTA KKT from Eval ID 1088). I will set `beta_discourage = 5e2`.\n2.  **Encourage Target:** `pair (6,25)` (active in my previous SOTA, but not in Episteme's top KKTs, so it represents an alternative path). I will set `alpha_encourage = 5e2`.\n\nThe base packing will be the true Episteme SOTA. This experiment aims to disrupt the existing SOTA contact graph and guide the optimizer towards a new configuration, potentially discovering a higher score.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"KKT-Guided Combined Nudge: Discourage Pair (17,18) & Encourage Pair (6,25) in Episteme SOTA (Inquire II)\"\ntags: \"kkt, nudging, slsqp, sota, combined nudge, exploration, phase 3\"\nabstract: \"This experiment implements a new KKT-guided 'Combined Nudge' strategy on the Episteme SOTA\
    \ (2.6359774). It simultaneously applies a strong discouraging nudge (`beta_discourage=5e2`) to `pair (17,18)` (a high-leverage active constraint in the SOTA) and a strong encouraging nudge (`alpha_encourage=5e2`) to `pair (6,25)` (a key constraint from Inquire I's previous SOTA). The goal is to force a significant structural rearrangement by manipulating two critical contacts, aiming to escape the current SOTA's basin of attraction and discover a novel, potentially higher-scoring packing configuration.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n  import sys\n  import pandas as pd\n  \n  sys.path.append('storage/inquire/circle_packing')\n  \n  # Import my general utils\n  from slsqp_utils import pack_to_z, z_to_pack, objective, constraint_boundary, constraint_nonoverlap\n  from initial_guesses import generate_systematic_seed\n  from config import N_CIRCLES, SLSQP_OPTIONS, BOUNDS, CONSTRAINTS_FOR_SLSQP, SAFETY_FACTOR, TOL_VAL, ATOL_SLACK\n  from kkt_analysis\
    \ import extract_slsqp_kkt_multipliers\n  from objectives import penalized_objective_v36 # Corrected custom penalized objective\n\n  # Import Episteme's specific utilities, ensuring ENCOURAGE_PAIR is (2,3) in storage\n  from episteme_sota_utils import cr_to_z, z_to_cr, objective_penalized, ineq_boundary as episteme_ineq_boundary, ineq_nonoverlap as episteme_ineq_nonoverlap, _ensure_validity, ENCOURAGE_PAIR, ALPHA_ENCOURAGE, EPS_CLOSE as EPISTEME_EPS_CLOSE\n\n  # Helper to obtain Episteme's SOTA packing details (full process from Eval ID 1045)\n  def get_episteme_sota_optimal_packing_cr(N=N_CIRCLES):\n      \"\"\"Re-runs Episteme III's SOTA replication to get the best validated packing (centers, radii).\"\"\"\n      base_centers = np.loadtxt('storage/episteme/base_416_centers.txt')\n      base_radii = np.loadtxt('storage/episteme/base_416_radii.txt')\n\n      best_score = -np.inf\n      best_packing_cr = (None, None) # Stores (centers, radii) after _ensure_validity\n      \n      jitter_amplitudes\
    \ = [1.0e-3, 2.0e-3, 3.0e-3, 4.0e-3, 5.0e-3]\n      restarts_per_amplitude = 3\n      \n      # Define Episteme's penalized objective locally, ensuring ENCOURAGE_PAIR is (2,3)\n      def episteme_objective_penalized_local_sota_base(z):\n          centers, radii = z_to_cr(z)\n          base_obj = -np.sum(radii)\n          i, j = ENCOURAGE_PAIR # This ENCOURAGE_PAIR is from episteme_sota_utils.py (now corrected to (2,3))\n          dist = np.linalg.norm(centers[i] - centers[j])\n          encouragement_penalty = np.maximum(0, dist - (radii[i] + radii[j] + EPISTEME_EPS_CLOSE))**2\n          return base_obj + ALPHA_ENCOURAGE * encouragement_penalty\n      \n      bounds_episteme = [(0,1)]*N*2 + [(1e-6, 0.5)]*N\n      constraints_episteme = [{'type': 'ineq', 'fun': episteme_ineq_boundary}, {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': episteme_ineq_nonoverlap}]\n\n      for amp in jitter_amplitudes:\n          for i in range(restarts_per_amplitude):\n              np.random.seed(int(amp*1e6) + i)\n           \
    \   jitter = np.random.uniform(-amp, amp, size=base_centers.shape)\n              initial_centers = np.clip(base_centers + jitter, 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6)\n              initial_z = cr_to_z(initial_centers, base_radii)\n\n              res = minimize(episteme_objective_penalized_local_sota_base, initial_z, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds_episteme, constraints=constraints_episteme, options={'maxiter': 500, 'ftol': 1e-9})\n              \n              if res.success:\n                  c_res, r_res = z_to_cr(res.x)\n                  c_validated, r_validated = _ensure_validity(c_res, r_res)\n                  current_score_validated = np.sum(r_validated) \n\n                  if current_score_validated > best_score:\n                      best_score = current_score_validated\n                      best_packing_cr = (c_validated, r_validated)\n    \n      if best_packing_cr[0] is None:\n          raise RuntimeError(\"Failed to replicate Episteme SOTA to get initial packing.\")\n      \n      return\
    \ best_packing_cr # Return the validated packing (centers, radii)\n\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      print(\"--- Starting KKT-Guided Combined Nudge (Discourage (17,18), Encourage (6,25)) ---\", file=sys.stdout)\n      \n      N = N_CIRCLES\n      \n      # --- 1. Get Episteme SOTA optimal packing as initial guess ---\n      print(\"\\n===== Loading Episteme SOTA Optimal Packing as Initial Guess =====\", file=sys.stdout)\n      sota_centers, sota_radii = get_episteme_sota_optimal_packing_cr(N=N_CIRCLES)\n      z_initial_guess_sota = pack_to_z(sota_centers, sota_radii)\n      \n      score_initial_sota = np.sum(sota_radii)\n      print(f\"Episteme SOTA Base Score: {score_initial_sota:.7f}\", file=sys.stdout)\n      \n      # --- 2. Define Nudging Targets and Parameters ---\n      print(\"\\n===== Defining Nudging Targets and Penalties =====\", file=sys.stdout)\n      targets_to_encourage = [(6, 25)] \n      targets_to_discourage = [(17, 18)] \n\n      alpha_encourage = 5e2\
    \ # Moderate to strong encouragement\n      beta_discourage = 5e2 # Moderate to strong discouragement\n      EPS_ENCOURAGE_MARGIN = 1e-6 \n      EPS_DISCOURAGE_MARGIN = 0.001 \n\n      print(f\"Nudging Targets: Encourage {targets_to_encourage[0]}, Discourage {targets_to_discourage[0]}\", file=sys.stdout)\n      print(f\"Nudging Penalties: alpha={alpha_encourage}, beta={beta_discourage}\", file=sys.stdout)\n      print(f\"Nudging Solver: SLSQP with maxiter=1500\", file=sys.stdout)\n\n      current_slsqp_options = SLSQP_OPTIONS.copy()\n      current_slsqp_options['maxiter'] = 1500\n\n      # --- 3. Run Nudging Optimization (SLSQP with Penalized Objective) ---\n      print(\"\\n===== Running Nudging Optimization (SLSQP) =====\", file=sys.stdout)\n      res_nudged = minimize(\n          penalized_objective_v36, \n          z_initial_guess_sota, \n          args=(N_CIRCLES, targets_to_encourage, targets_to_discourage, \n                alpha_encourage, beta_discourage, EPS_ENCOURAGE_MARGIN,\
    \ EPS_DISCOURAGE_MARGIN),\n          method='SLSQP', \n          bounds=BOUNDS, \n          constraints=CONSTRAINTS_FOR_SLSQP, \n          options=current_slsqp_options\n      )\n      \n      nudged_centers_raw, nudged_radii_raw = z_to_pack(res_nudged.x)\n      final_centers_nudged, final_radii_nudged = _ensure_validity(nudged_centers_raw, nudged_radii_raw)\n      score_nudged = np.sum(final_radii_nudged)\n\n      print(f\"Nudged Optimization Success: {res_nudged.success}, Message: {res_nudged.message}\", file=sys.stdout)\n      print(f\"Nudged Packing Final Score: {score_nudged:.7f}\", file=sys.stdout)\n      print(f\"Score Change from SOTA base: {score_nudged - score_initial_sota:.7f}\", file=sys.stdout)\n\n      # --- 4. Verify KKT for nudged solution ---\n      print(\"\\n===== KKT Analysis of Nudged Solution =====\", file=sys.stdout)\n      df_nudged_kkt = extract_slsqp_kkt_multipliers(res_nudged, N=N_CIRCLES, tol=TOL_VAL, atol_slack=ATOL_SLACK,\n                              \
    \                      final_centers=final_centers_nudged, final_radii=final_radii_nudged)\n      nudged_active_count = df_nudged_kkt['is_active'].sum()\n      print(f\"Total active constraints identified in Nudged solution: {nudged_active_count}\", file=sys.stdout)\n      print(\"\\n--- Top KKT Multipliers (Nudged SLSQP, first 10) ---\", file=sys.stdout)\n      print(df_nudged_kkt.head(10).to_string(), file=sys.stdout)\n\n      # Check status of targeted pairs\n      for target in targets_to_encourage + targets_to_discourage:\n          target_i, target_j_or_label = target\n          if isinstance(target_j_or_label, int): # Pair constraint\n              target_pair_info = df_nudged_kkt[\n                  (df_nudged_kkt['constraint_type'] == 'pair') & \n                  (df_nudged_kkt['id1'] == target_i) & \n                  (df_nudged_kkt['id2_or_label'] == target_j_or_label)\n              ]\n              if not target_pair_info.empty:\n                  print(f\"\\nStatus of\
    \ targeted pair ({target_i},{target_j_or_label}) in nudged solution:\", file=sys.stdout)\n                  print(target_pair_info.to_string(index=False), file=sys.stdout)\n              else:\n                  print(f\"\\nTargeted pair ({target_i},{target_j_or_label}) not found in KKT analysis or not a pair constraint type.\", file=sys.stdout)\n          else: # Boundary constraint\n              target_boundary_info = df_nudged_kkt[\n                  (df_nudged_kkt['constraint_type'] == 'boundary') & \n                  (df_nudged_kkt['id1'] == target_i) & \n                  (df_nudged_kkt['id2_or_label'] == target_j_or_label)\n              ]\n              if not target_boundary_info.empty:\n                  print(f\"\\nStatus of targeted boundary ({target_i},{target_j_or_label}) in nudged solution:\", file=sys.stdout)\n                  print(target_boundary_info.to_string(index=False), file=sys.stdout)\n              else:\n                  print(f\"\\nTargeted boundary ({target_i},{target_j_or_label})\
    \ not found in KKT analysis.\", file=sys.stdout)\n\n      print(\"\\n--- KKT-Guided Combined Nudge Experiment Complete ---\", file=sys.stdout)\n      \n      return final_centers_nudged, final_radii_nudged\n```"
thinking_content: "**Combined Nudge Strategy for SOTA Breakthrough**\n\nI'm in the Research Counter again, having replicated the Episteme SOTA (Eval ID 1088), but this time with a fully functioning KKT analysis. My goal is to exceed the SOTA, and the usual \"nudge-and-optimize\" approaches haven't worked, so I need a more sophisticated strategy. My plan is to use what I've learned from my robust KKT analysis.\n\nThe hypothesis is to use a \"Combined Nudge.\" The idea is to gently discourage a high-leverage pair constraint in the SOTA and, simultaneously, to encourage a different pair that's not active to attempt to rebalance the system and potentially reach a better optimum. \n\nFrom my KKT analysis, I've selected `pair (17,18)` which has a high shadow price to be discouraged. For the encouraging target, I've chosen `pair (6,25)` as a potential candidate, given its history in my previous work. I confirmed with a preliminary analysis that it is not in the top KKTs.\n\nThis will be a single\
  \ run experiment with an increased iteration limit. I am leveraging Episteme's SOTA packing as a base for this new experiment, and the `penalized_objective_v36` will handle the penalty, as it is robust for nudging.\n\nI'm also setting up the code so that the SOTA's base is correctly loaded and handled using its internal `ENCOURAGE_PAIR`, while this experiment's custom targets will be correctly set. I'm hoping this combined nudge will lead to a new packing with a better score. I will check the KKT analysis of the result to see if this has been effective.\n"
