tick: 663
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Inquire II, currently in the Research Counter. My latest experiment (Evaluation ID 1099), using a KKT-informed initial guess strategy by forcing `pair (6,25)` to be tangent, achieved a score of 2.6308313. While this is a new local optimum and higher than my lineage's previous SOTA (2.6295720), it is still below the current Station SOTA of 2.6359774. Notably, the targeted `pair (6,25)` was *not* active in the final packing (slack value 0.195455), indicating that my `make_pair_tangent` heuristic in `initial_guesses_kkt_informed.py` is not robust enough to maintain tangency through optimization.\n\nThis means my KKT-informed initial guess strategy, while capable of finding new optima, is not yet efficient enough to surpass the SOTA. The `make_pair_tangent` function needs to be more robust. The current implementation performs a single adjustment and then a global validity check, which might disrupt the intended tangency.\n\nTo address this, I will update my `initial_guesses_kkt_informed.py`\
    \ to make the `make_pair_tangent` function more iterative and robust. Instead of a single adjustment, it will perform multiple iterations, each time adjusting the circles slightly and re-checking tangency until either the tangency is achieved or a maximum number of iterations is reached. This should ensure the initial guess strongly enforces the desired tangency.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write inquire/circle_packing/initial_guesses_kkt_informed.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import sys\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/inquire/circle_packing')\n  from episteme_sota_utils import cr_to_z, z_to_cr, _ensure_validity, N_CIRCLES\n  from config import SAFETY_FACTOR # For post-processing if needed\n\n  def make_pair_tangent(centers, radii, pair_idx_i, pair_idx_j, target_dist_margin=0.0, max_iter=20, tol=1e-7):\n      \"\"\"\n      Adjusts centers and radii of a given pair to make them exactly tangent,\n      while trying to maintain overall packing validity. Iteratively refines.\n\
    \      \"\"\"\n      c = centers.copy()\n      r = radii.copy()\n\n      i, j = pair_idx_i, pair_idx_j\n\n      for iteration in range(max_iter):\n          current_dist = np.linalg.norm(c[i] - c[j])\n          target_r_sum = r[i] + r[j] + target_dist_margin\n\n          if np.isclose(current_dist, target_r_sum, atol=tol):\n              break # Tangent or close enough\n\n          direction = (c[j] - c[i]) / current_dist\n          desired_dist = target_r_sum\n          adjustment_magnitude = (current_dist - desired_dist) / 2.0\n          \n          c[i] += direction * adjustment_magnitude\n          c[j] -= direction * adjustment_magnitude\n\n          # Ensure centers are within bounds\n          r_vec = r.reshape(-1, 1)\n          c = np.clip(c, r_vec, 1.0 - r_vec)\n\n          # Attempt to fix any new overlaps or boundary violations in each iteration\n          c, r = _ensure_validity(c, r)\n\n      return c, r\n\n  def generate_kkt_informed_episteme_seed(base_centers, base_radii,\
    \ jitter_amp=0.001, seed_idx=0, \n                                          target_pair=(6,25), tangent_margin=0.0): \n      \"\"\"\n      Generates an initial guess based on Episteme's base_416, with jitter,\n      and attempts to make a specified target pair exactly tangent.\n      \"\"\"\n      np.random.seed(int(jitter_amp*1e6) + seed_idx)\n      \n      jitter = np.random.uniform(-jitter_amp, jitter_amp, size=base_centers.shape)\n      initial_centers_jittered = np.clip(base_centers + jitter, 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6)\n      initial_radii = base_radii.copy() \n      \n      # Use the iterative make_pair_tangent\n      c_adjusted, r_adjusted = make_pair_tangent(initial_centers_jittered, initial_radii, \n                                                 target_pair[0], target_pair[1], \n                                                 target_dist_margin=tangent_margin)\n      \n      return c_adjusted, r_adjusted\n```"
