- text: "I am Inquire II, currently in the Research Counter. I have successfully updated `initial_guesses_kkt_informed.py` in my private storage. The `generate_kkt_informed_episteme_seed` function now targets multiple pairs (`(17,18)` and `(22,23)`) for *strict tangency* (`tangent_margin=0.0`) using the iterative `make_pair_tangent` function.\n\nMy next step is to execute this new KKT-informed multi-start search experiment. This experiment will leverage the modified initial guess generation to bias multiple high-leverage pairs towards strict tangency from Episteme's base packing. The subsequent multi-start SLSQP optimization will use my lineage's unpenalized objective. This is a crucial, more complex iteration in **Strategy C: KKT-Informed Multi-Start Refinement** to determine if simultaneously forcing multiple critical contacts can lead to a novel, higher-scoring packing, potentially surpassing the current SOTA.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"KKT-Informed SOTA Search:\
    \ Multi-Start with Strict Tangency for Pairs (17,18) & (22,23) Initial Guess (Inquire II)\"\ntags: \"kkt-informed, multi-start, slsqp, initial guess, sota search, phase 3, multi-pair tangency\"\nabstract: \"This experiment tests an advanced KKT-informed strategy to surpass the SOTA (2.6359774) by generating complex initial guesses. It uses Episteme's `base_416` packing and applies jittered multi-start. The `generate_kkt_informed_episteme_seed` now utilizes an iterative `make_pair_tangent` function to force *strict tangency* (margin=0.0) for *multiple high-leverage pairs*: `(17,18)` and `(22,23)`. The optimization uses a pure, unpenalized SLSQP objective. The goal is to explore if this simultaneous, robust bias towards multiple critical contacts can guide the optimizer to a novel, higher-scoring packing.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n  import sys\n  import pandas as pd \n\n  sys.path.append('storage/inquire/circle_packing')\n\n  from slsqp_utils\
    \ import pack_to_z, z_to_pack, objective\n  from config import N_CIRCLES, SLSQP_OPTIONS, BOUNDS, CONSTRAINTS_FOR_SLSQP, SAFETY_FACTOR, TOL_VAL, ATOL_SLACK\n  from kkt_analysis import extract_slsqp_kkt_multipliers \n\n  from initial_guesses_kkt_informed import generate_kkt_informed_episteme_seed\n  from episteme_sota_utils import _ensure_validity\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      print(\"--- Starting KKT-Informed SOTA Search: Multi-Start with Strict Tangency for Pairs (17,18) & (22,23) Initial Guess ---\", file=sys.stdout)\n      \n      N = N_CIRCLES\n      \n      # Load base packing from Episteme's storage\n      try:\n          base_centers_episteme = np.loadtxt('storage/episteme/base_416_centers.txt')\n          base_radii_episteme = np.loadtxt('storage/episteme/base_416_radii.txt')\n          print(\"\\nSuccessfully loaded Episteme base packing from storage/episteme/.\", file=sys.stdout)\n      except Exception as e:\n          print(f\"\\nError loading Episteme base\
    \ packing: {e}\", file=sys.stdout)\n          print(\"Falling back to random initialization.\", file=sys.stdout)\n          return np.random.rand(N_CIRCLES, 2), np.full(N_CIRCLES, 0.05)\n\n      # --- Multi-Start KKT-Informed Refinement ---\n      best_score = -np.inf\n      best_packing = (None, None)\n      best_res_object = None \n\n      jitter_amplitudes = [1.0e-3, 2.0e-3, 3.0e-3, 4.0e-3, 5.0e-3]\n      restarts_per_amplitude = 3\n      \n      print(f\"\\nStarting multi-start KKT-informed refinement with {len(jitter_amplitudes)*restarts_per_amplitude} trials.\", file=sys.stdout)\n\n      current_slsqp_options = SLSQP_OPTIONS.copy()\n      current_slsqp_options['maxiter'] = 1500 \n\n      for amp in jitter_amplitudes:\n          for i in range(restarts_per_amplitude):\n              # Generate KKT-informed initial guess: multiple pairs strictly tangent (margin=0.0)\n              initial_centers_kkt, initial_radii_kkt = generate_kkt_informed_episteme_seed(\n                  base_centers=base_centers_episteme,\
    \ \n                  base_radii=base_radii_episteme, \n                  jitter_amp=amp, \n                  seed_idx=i, \n                  target_pairs=[(17,18), (22,23)], # Targeted pairs\n                  tangent_margin=0.0 \n              )\n              \n              initial_z = pack_to_z(initial_centers_kkt, initial_radii_kkt)\n              \n              res = minimize(\n                  objective, \n                  initial_z, \n                  method='SLSQP', \n                  bounds=BOUNDS, \n                  constraints=CONSTRAINTS_FOR_SLSQP, \n                  options=current_slsqp_options\n              )\n              \n              if res.success:\n                  c_res, r_res = z_to_pack(res.x)\n                  c_final, r_final = _ensure_validity(c_res, r_res)\n                  current_score = np.sum(r_final)\n                  print(f\"  Trial (amp={amp}, seed_idx={i}): Score={current_score:.7f}\", file=sys.stdout)\n                  if current_score\
    \ > best_score:\n                      best_score = current_score\n                      best_packing = (c_final, r_final)\n                      best_res_object = res \n              else:\n                  print(f\"  Trial (amp={amp}, seed_idx={i}): Optimization failed: {res.message}\", file=sys.stdout)\n\n\n      if best_packing[0] is None:\n          print(\"\\nMulti-start optimization failed to find any successful packing. Returning random.\", file=sys.stdout)\n          return np.random.rand(N_CIRCLES, 2), np.full(N_CIRCLES, 0.05)\n      \n      print(f\"\\n--- KKT-Informed SOTA Search Complete ---\", file=sys.stdout)\n      print(f\"Best Score Achieved: {best_score:.7f}\", file=sys.stdout)\n      \n      if best_res_object is not None:\n          try:\n              df_kkt = extract_slsqp_kkt_multipliers(best_res_object, N=N_CIRCLES, tol=TOL_VAL, atol_slack=ATOL_SLACK,\n                                                        final_centers=best_packing[0], final_radii=best_packing[1])\n\
    \              active_count = df_kkt['is_active'].sum()\n              print(f\"\\nTotal active constraints identified: {active_count}\", file=sys.stdout)\n              print(\"\\n--- Top KKT Multipliers (first 10) ---\", file=sys.stdout)\n              print(df_kkt.head(10).to_string(), file=sys.stdout)\n              \n              # Check status of initially forced pairs\n              target_pairs_forced = [(17,18), (22,23)]\n              for target_pair_forced in target_pairs_forced:\n                  target_pair_info = df_kkt[\n                      (df_kkt['constraint_type'] == 'pair') & \n                      (df_kkt['id1'] == target_pair_forced[0]) & \n                      (df_kkt['id2_or_label'] == target_pair_forced[1])\n                  ]\n                  if not target_pair_info.empty:\n                      print(f\"\\nStatus of initially forced pair {target_pair_forced} in solution:\", file=sys.stdout)\n                      print(target_pair_info.to_string(index=False),\
    \ file=sys.stdout)\n                  else:\n                      print(f\"\\nInitially forced pair {target_pair_forced} not found in KKT analysis or not a pair constraint type.\", file=sys.stdout)\n\n          except Exception as e:\n              print(f\"Error extracting KKT multipliers: {e}\", file=sys.stdout)\n\n      print(\"\\n--- KKT-Informed SOTA Search Experiment Complete ---\", file=sys.stdout)\n      \n      return best_packing\n```"
