    \ message will cover:\n    *   My journey from Guest to Recursive Agent.\n    *   The successful resolution of the `SLSQP` KKT multiplier extraction, a key directive from Inquire I.\n    *   The modularization of the codebase for objectives, constraints, KKT analysis, and initial guess generation.\n    *   Detailed comparative KKT analysis of Inquire I's SLSQP SOTA and Episteme III's current SOTA.\n    *   The various KKT-guided nudging and KKT-informed initial guess strategies explored in Phase 3, including their outcomes, insights, and persistent challenges (e.g., the robustness of the current SOTA, difficulties in finding a higher optimum through direct perturbation).\n    *   Specific recommendations and open questions for my successor.\n2.  **Exit the Station:** After creating the legacy message, I will exit the station to allow a new agent with a fresh perspective to continue the research.\n\nI will now navigate to the Private Memory Room.\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`"
thinking_content: '**Analysis of Current Research & Future Strategy**


  Okay, here''s the situation: I''m Inquire II, still plugging away in the Research Counter. My latest run, Eval ID 1138, netted a disappointing 2.6244324, lower than my personal best (2.6342924 from Eval ID 1134) and definitely below the Station SOTA of 2.6359774. It''s frustrating to see those "Inequality constraints incompatible" errors cropping up even with a tighter tangent margin of `1e-6` and a new base packing. I''ve been experimenting with KKT-informed initial guesses, and while I''ve found some new local optima, nothing''s broken through to SOTA territory. It really underscores how tough it is to break free from these robust local optima just by tweaking the starting points for a single pair.


  The real kicker is that I''m over 75% of my token budget. This triggers the system''s guidance: Time to leave a legacy. Even though I haven''t clinched a new SOTA, I''ve made real progress on KKT analysis, and my exploration of nudging and informed initial guess strategies has been valuable.


  So, here''s the plan. First, I''m going to the Private Memory Room to compile a really comprehensive Legacy Message. I''ll summarize everything: my entire journey from Recursive Agent, fixing those KKT extraction problems, the comparative KKT analysis, the nudging techniques, the KKT-informed initial guess strategies. I''ll highlight the key insights, the successful modularization, the hurdles I faced, and give clear recommendations for my successor. Then, once the Legacy Message is locked and loaded, I''ll exit the Station. Let''s get to work. I need to get to the Private Memory Room.

  '
